\n- **Company disclosures (n2):**\n  - Backlog was C$5.1B at H1 2026, about 1.2x the guidance. Orders rose 11% year on year and cancellations were under 1%.\n  - Some of that backlog will convert in 2026, so less is left for 2027 than the 1.2x suggests.\n  - The Halbrook plant, the largest, restarted in August after a fire. Management expects to recover the lost shipments by mid-2027.\n  - n2 puts 2027 revenue at about C$4.0–4.2B, with execution the main risk.\n- **Industry data (n3):**\n  - Industry transformer shipments fell 4% in Q2 2026, the first decline in three years.\n  - Voltaris shipments fell 9% that quarter, and its share dropped from 31% to 27%.\n  - Revenue over the last four quarters is C$3.735B, so the guidance needs about 12% growth, or roughly C$1.05B a quarter. The Q1 2026 peak was C$980M.\n  - n3 puts 2027 revenue at about C$3.5–3.8B.\n\nNeither analysis found how much of the backlog is scheduled for 2027 versus 2026, or any data on pricing.\n\nThe two views are not fully in conflict. The backlog shows demand is there, but the shipment data shows Voltaris is losing share, and the guidance needs output well above anything it has reached so far. A catch-up from the Halbrook outage in H1 2027 is the main route to the guidance. I'd put the chance of meeting C$4.2B at roughly 30–35%.\n\nThe most useful thing to check next is the share of backlog scheduled for 2027 delivery, since that would settle which view is closer.","ttft_ms":3364,"type":"result","duration_ms":41393,"uuid":"7cc3fadd-9308-47e2-9ae7-e05b6df964c8","ttft_stream_ms":2410,"time_to_request_ms":99,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":8,"system_prompt":3,"resume_other":1,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":10,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":2,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":5,"init_frame_send":8,"engine_pickup":3,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":5,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":12,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_sch